# Tests and fixtures

Guardrails: G-02, G-03, G-12

## Fake values: narrow exception (G-02)

- Obviously fake numeric values are allowed only inside unit tests of deterministic arithmetic.
- Use clearly fake names such as "TEST BORROWER A" or "TEST BDC 1".
- Never use real borrower names, real BDC data, or realistic-looking financial data in
  tests, fixtures, seeds, UI, demos, or shipped application code.

```ts
// GOOD (unit test of arithmetic only)
expect(ratio({ name: "TEST BORROWER A", fairValue: 90, principal: 100 })).toBe(0.9);
```

## Database tests: second narrow exception (G-02)

- Obviously fake structural values are also allowed inside `db/tests/*.sql`, which exercise
  constraints and triggers. Each file runs in one transaction that the runner rolls back,
  and the runner fails if any table's row count changes.
- Fake values must be unmistakable: names like "TEST BDC 1", CIKs `9999999901` and up,
  accession numbers `0000000000-00-0000NN`, dates in 2099, URLs under
  `https://www.sec.gov/files/TEST-ONLY/`, and small round amounts.
- Test files never contain transaction control (`BEGIN;`, `COMMIT;`, `ROLLBACK;`); the
  runner owns the transaction.
- Nothing from `db/tests/` may become a seed, a migration, a committed dump, or data in any
  non-ephemeral database.

## Pipeline synthetic fixtures (G-02)

- Obviously fake registry and filing-history payloads are also allowed in
  `fixtures/pipeline/**` and `pipeline/test/**` so parsers and the offline loader can run
  without the network.
- The same markers apply: "TEST BDC", CIKs `9999999901` and up, accessions
  `0000000000-00-0000NN`, dates in 2099, and `TEST-ONLY` URLs. A guard test refuses
  committed synthetic files that lack those markers or that contain realistic BDC names.
- Pipeline tests never take a registrant CIK from an accession-number prefix.

## Real SEC source files (G-02, G-03, G-12)

- Real SEC files are downloaded only into the git-ignored `.cache/sec/` (source-schema
  fixtures) or `.data/sec/` (registry fetch store) by `npm run sec:fetch` /
  `npm run registry:fetch`. They are never committed, copied, or excerpted into the
  repository.
- The repository holds only `fixtures/sec/manifest.json` (source URL, retrieval time,
  HTTP metadata, SHA-256) and structure-only snapshots in `fixtures/sec/snapshots/`:
  headers, counts, and format classes, with no registrant or borrower names and no
  financial values.
- Tests that need real SEC content read it from `.cache/sec/` or `.data/sec/` and skip
  when it is absent. CI uses synthetic fixtures only and is network-free.
- Fixtures and snapshots may only describe fields documented in `docs/SOURCE_SCHEMAS.md`.
- Never record the `SEC_USER_AGENT` value anywhere in the repository.

## Seeds

- Seeds may contain reference enumerations only (for example, state names). Never
  financial or borrower data.
